<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="018" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-04 privilege derivation from communications (owner option A widened)</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>after 015; hard gate of 022</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies SignalReadService.cs and the capability (.cs); privacy-sensitive (FR-04, ADR-015)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Confidentiality control: a wrong derivation leaks privileged legal detail to the model through 022; fail-closed semantics across fault, 403 and unreadable rows must be exact</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns SignalReadService.cs, DecideLanePaging.cs, WorklistItemSummary.cs, DecisionCapability.cs and the new WorkItemPrivilege.cs in its wave; 020 and 021 touch none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>015</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, privacy, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Derive the Decide-lane privilege flag at read time from communications, as the caller, per the owner's ruling of 2026-11-08 (option A widened): a Work Item is privilege-flagged when its subject (when the subject is a sprk_communication) or any of its witness or evidence communications has sprk_communication.sprk_privilegeclassification Privileged or Potentially Privileged. Replace task 015's read of sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged (never written, ontology DI-64) with this derivation, in one injectable helper in Services/Signals/ that ontology DI-143 (#2630) can reuse for the Decision Record snapshot.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in caller-scoped Dataverse Web API reads, fail-closed access rules and batched query bounds.</role>
  <goal>WorklistItemSummary.PrivilegeFlagged on every Decide-lane page equals the derivation rule below, computed with one batched caller read of sprk_communication per page (per 200 distinct communication ids), failing closed; the Console's REST worklist response is unchanged byte for byte; the helper has a public method ontology DI-143 can call.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-04 as amended 2026-11-08; notes/decisions.md entries 'Task 015', 'Ontology review of 015' and 'Owner ruling FR-04 (2026-11-08)'. Task 015 selects sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged in the Lanes FetchXML and carries it through WorklistItemExtras to the summary; that column has no production writer (ontology DI-64), so every summary reads false today. The D-142 batched witness read (SignalReadService.WitnessesTheCallerReadsAsync, the caller read before SignalSuppressionService.WitnessDetailShownOnReadAsync) and EarlierInvoiceReadability (public helper, caller client passed in, chunks of 200, 403 = verdict, 401/5xx/unparseable/nextLink/exception = fault) are the shapes to copy. Option values (CommunicationPrivilegeClassification): None 100000000, Potentially Privileged 100000001, Privileged 100000002. Owner ruling 2026-07-16: privilege never gates a read on its own; this flag only reduces model-visible text, in task 022.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/WorkItemPrivilege.cs (the injectable helper and its sources record)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs (WorklistItemExtras carries the privilege sources instead of the column; the Lanes query stops selecting sprk_privilegeflagged)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecideLanePaging.cs (summaries start flagged: fail closed until derived)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCapability.cs (ListDecidePageAsync derives the page's flags with one batched read)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/WorklistItemSummary.cs (PrivilegeFlagged doc: the derivation, not the column)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SignalsModule.cs (register WorkItemPrivilege, scoped, unconditional)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Signals/WorkItemPrivilegeTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/regression/Signals/DecideLanePagingTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests/Signals/SignalReadRouteTests.cs (World: a communication with a classification; CommunicationType in the catalog)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs (WitnessesTheCallerReadsAsync, D-142: batched caller read, 403 verdict vs 401 fault)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/EarlierInvoiceReadability.cs (public reusable caller-read helper, ShownAsync&lt;TKey&gt;, ReadAsCallerAsync)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Access/CommunicationAccessModels.cs (CommunicationPrivilegeClassification values)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="015" status="completed">WorklistItemSummary, WorklistItemExtras, DecideLanePaging and ListDecidePageAsync</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-11-08">A Decide item is privilege-flagged when its subject, when the subject is a sprk_communication, or any of its witness or evidence communications (an evidence line whose ref is sprk_communication:{id}) has sprk_communication.sprk_privilegeclassification = Privileged (100000002) or Potentially Privileged (100000001). None (100000000) and null are NOT flagged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-11-08">The flag is derived at read time AS THE CALLER through IDataverseUserClient, with no app-only fallback, in one batched read per page (In lists of at most 200 ids, shaped like D-142's batched witness read). A read FAULT (exception, 5xx, 401, throttling, unparseable body, a body with @odata.nextLink) flags every item that needed the read; a communication the caller cannot read (not returned, or a 403 on the table) flags its item (fail closed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-11-08">sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged is NOT a source (never written, ontology DI-64): the Lanes query stops selecting it and nothing reads it for the flag.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-11-08">The helper lives in Services/Signals/ as an injectable type with a clear public method, and its remarks document the reuse by ontology DI-143 (#2630) for the Decision Record snapshot.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-07-16">Privilege never gates a read on its own: no row is dropped, added or reordered by the flag, and no response other than the slim page changes; the flag only reduces model-visible text, in task 022.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Minimum text: the derivation reads only the id and the classification of each communication; nothing it reads is returned except the boolean flag.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The REST responses of GET /api/v1/signals/worklist, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision-plan, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/suppression and POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision stay byte-for-byte unchanged: task 011's contract baseline tests pass with no golden-file edit (FR-09); the REST worklist adds no request.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every read this task adds is the caller's (the IDataverseUserClient the capability already holds); a null or unauthenticated caller stays DataverseUserClientErrorCodes.UserContextRequired before any read (FR-10 option C). No ICallerContext, no app-only client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every PR from this task that touches Services/Signals/** is reviewed by spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 before merge (project CLAUDE.md §4); the commit body says so.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">The new type and its DI registration carry the three-question component justification (existing, extension, cost of doing nothing) in the file header.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries (IDataverseUserClient), and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
