      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/decisions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Dataverse $select is all-or-nothing" location=".claude/FAILURE-MODES.md">G-13: a wrong column name fails the whole read; sprk_privilegeclassification on sprk_communication is verified live (messaging-communication-app-r1 schema spec) and read by CommunicationAccessFilter.</pattern>
      <pattern name="401 is a fault, 403 is a verdict" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs">DataverseUserClient maps 401 and 403 to AccessDenied; only a 403 means "no Read on the table".</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Create WorkItemPrivilege (Services/Signals/): a public static SourcesOf(subjectTable, subjectId, storedEvidence) building WorkItemPrivilegeSources (communication ids; Undetermined when the subject's table is unknown or the evidence cannot be judged), and a public FlaggedAsync&lt;TKey&gt;(IDataverseUserClient caller, items, ct) returning the flagged keys with the fail-closed rules above.</step>
    <step order="2">SignalReadService: WorklistItemExtras carries the sources (subject table from the catalog, the stored evidence as read) instead of the column; the Lanes query no longer selects sprk_privilegeflagged; nothing else in the pipeline changes.</step>
    <step order="3">DecideLanePaging builds summaries flagged (fail closed until derived); DecisionCapability.ListDecidePageAsync calls FlaggedAsync once for the page's items with its caller client and sets each summary's flag.</step>
    <step order="4">Register WorkItemPrivilege in SignalsModule (scoped, unconditional) with the justification comment.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the tests in the acceptance criteria; update the 015 paging seed to mark privilege through communications.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the Signals, WorklistItemSummary and ContractBaseline unit filters, the Signal integration filter and ArchTests; measure the publish-size delta from fresh worktrees; run the vulnerable-package check.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If sprk_privilegeclassification is not readable as the caller through the sprk_communications entity set (wrong set or column name), STOP and escalate with the evidence (FAILURE-MODES G-13).</trigger>
    <trigger>If meeting the one-batched-read-per-page bound would require changing the REST worklist's requests or response, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any acceptance criterion would require privilege to drop, add or reorder a row (a read gate), STOP: owner ruling 2026-07-16 wins; escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>WorklistItemExtras.PrivilegeFlagged (task 015) reads sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged, which nothing writes (DI-64); CommunicationAccessFilter reads sprk_privilegeclassification for one communication route's rows, and the D-142 witness read and EarlierInvoiceReadability are batched caller reads of other columns and tables.</existing>
    <extension>The D-142 read is private, selects only the key and is keyed on lineage tables; EarlierInvoiceReadability judges invoices only; CommunicationAccessFilter decides visibility per thread row, not a flag per Work Item. This adds the one rule (subject + witness communications, fail closed) as a reusable helper in the same shape, so DI-143 does not copy it.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every summary's PrivilegeFlagged stays false, so task 022 reduces nothing and privileged communication subjects and titles reach model-visible text (FR-04, ADR-015); 022 is hard-gated on this task.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/WorkItemPrivilege.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCapability.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Signals/WorkItemPrivilegeTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/regression/Signals/DecideLanePagingTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">(a) An item whose subject is a sprk_communication classified Privileged, and one classified Potentially Privileged, are each PrivilegeFlagged = true.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(b) An item whose subject is not a communication but whose evidence quotes a Privileged (or Potentially Privileged) communication is PrivilegeFlagged = true.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(c) Negative: an item whose communications (subject and witnesses) are all classified None, or have a null classification, is PrivilegeFlagged = false.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(d) Negative: when the caller's classification read faults (5xx, 401, throttling, unparseable body, @odata.nextLink, exception), every item with a communication is PrivilegeFlagged = true, items with no communication are false, the page is still returned, and a Warning names the table and the error code only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(e) Negative: a communication the caller cannot read (not returned by the read, or a 403 on the table) flags its item.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(f) Negative: an item whose subject is not a communication and whose evidence quotes no communication is PrivilegeFlagged = false, and a page made only of such items makes no classification read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(g) One batched caller read per page: a 50-item page whose items name communications makes exactly one sprk_communications classification read (In list, ids deduplicated); more than 200 distinct ids on one page are read in chunks of 200 (count pinned); the REST worklist makes no classification read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(h) FR-04 done-when: an item whose subject is a Privileged communication, seeded with a unique marker in its title and subject name, is PrivilegeFlagged = true on its summary. Asserting that the marker is absent from the model-visible text of spaarke_show_decisions is task 022's test (022 does the reduction).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged is not a source: the Lanes query does not select it, and a Signal whose stored column is true with a None communication subject is not flagged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">011's worklist baseline passes with no golden change; the one-batched-BillingEventRead test passes; paging order, page sizes and the stale-cursor tests are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE), the adversarial review and the ontology review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Owner ruling 2026-11-08: option A widened (notes/decisions.md). Task 022 is hard-gated on this task. Ontology DI-143 (#2630) reuses WorkItemPrivilege for the Decision Record snapshot.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
